@component gateway-client-key-mgmt
@intent KEY-MGMT client-side sub-module of the `gateway-client` runtime adapter family (v1.1 split per phase_2 2026-06-04). Distills `Constellation.md §13.16.11` (KEY-MGMT client-side discipline, v2.5.1+ cycle_b ship + UI 5 key mgmt window) into a formal eux contract — previously implicit in the parent gateway-client.eux, now formalized as a first-class sub-module per phase_2 scope expansion. Owns the client-side surface of the KEY-MGMT family: (a) KeyIssue request / response cycle (operator issues new upstream key uk-* or collab key ck-*; server stamps + returns), (b) KeyList query (display issued keys + connection status + label), (c) KeyRevoke (immediate session-end discriminator — immediate kills active connections, sessionEnd waits for natural close), (d) KeyLabel + AgentNameChanged broadcast (label edits propagate via server-mediated broadcast so all connected boards reflect), (e) KEY-MGMT legacy v0.2 transitional alias deprecation (per v2.5.13 KEY-MGMT §3.1 — supersede + transitional alias + deprecated v0.2 + no-fixed-version retire, zero-traffic gated). Client gateway exposes these as command-tier ports for the host application (UI or programmatic).
@expansion temperature=0.2 model=agent/claude template=estreux/v0.1
@targets vanilla
@profile protocol-adapter
@source Constellation.md(v2.3.21+ §13.16.11 KEY-MGMT client-side discipline) · constellation/reference/runtime/server.cjs(L188-360 KEY-MGMT block) · WS-PROTOCOL §13.16.11 KEY-MGMT semantics
@wire
  # field names aligned to the reference server + WS-PROTOCOL-KEY-MGMT.md v0.5 (Constellation v2.4.167). Selector: keyRef (non-secret) preferred, key accepted for compatibility; keyRef is the only selector for kind local.
  key_mgmt_messages:
    KeyIssue:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [label, kind? (upstream|collab|local|peer — closed, unknown → UNKNOWN_KIND), ttlDays? (15|30|90; absent → kind default), ttl? (ms, compatibility — same set), roleDescription?, boundAgent?]
      response: server emits KeyIssued{key (null for local), keyRef, label, kind, ttl, issuedAt, expiresAt, joinUrl?, joinUrls?, joinHint? (local)} · errors INVALID_TTL (outside the set, incl. 0) / UNKNOWN_KIND / INVALID_LABEL / LIMIT_EXCEEDED
    KeyList:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [includeRevoked?, includeDeleted?]
      response: server emits KeyListResult{keys[]: {key (null for local), keyRef, label, kind, state, phase (active|standby|dormant|revoking|revoked|deleted), ttl, ttlDays?, ttlChoices, issuedAt, renewedAt, renewCount, expiresAt, graceUntil?, revokedAt, lapsed, lastAgent, lastSeenAt, connectionStatus, roleDescription, adoptedFromLegacy}}
    KeyRevoke:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [keyRef | key, mode (immediate|sessionEnd)]
      response: server emits KeyRevoked{key, mode, agentsDisconnected, agentsNotified}; accepted in phases active / standby / dormant; ALREADY_REVOKED only for revoked / deleted
    KeyLabel:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [keyRef | key, newLabel]
      response: server emits KeyLabeled{key, oldLabel, newLabel}; unicasts AgentNameChanged to live holders of the key
    KeyRenew:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [keyRef | key, ttlDays? (15|30|90) | ttl?]
      response: server emits KeyRenewed{key (null for local), keyRef, label, kind, ttl, issuedAt, renewedAt, expiresAt, wasLapsed, renewCount}; key string unchanged · NOT_RENEWABLE (revoked/revoking/deleted) · NO_EXPIRY (ttl 0)
    KeyPurge:
      type: CUSTOM
      value_fields: [keyRefs? (absent → every revoked row not in REVOKED_PENDING)]
      response: server emits KeyPurged{count, keyRefs, error?}; rows become tombstones (key null, state DELETED)
    AgentNameChanged:
      type: CUSTOM
      direction: server → live holders of the relabelled key (unicast, one frame per connection)
      value_fields: [key, oldLabel, newLabel]
      effect: the holder MAY update its own agentName and re-announce
    ConnectionRejected (key-expired):
      type: CUSTOM
      direction: server → the connecting client (source server)
      value_fields: [code key-expired, phase (standby|dormant), renewable (request|operator), graceUntil? (standby), label, expiresAt, hint]
      effect: standby + renewable request → reconnecting with the renewal marker renews the key; dormant → only the board operator can renew (report once, do not retry faster than the refusal backoff)
  renewal_marker:                                          # v2.4.167 §13.25.19 — send on every connection attempt; no effect outside standby
    url_key: query parameter renew=1
    hello_body_key: HELLO field renewRequest true
  legacy_v0_2_alias_deprecation:                          # per v2.5.13 KEY-MGMT §3.1
    state: supersede + transitional alias + deprecated v0.2 + no-fixed-version retire
    retire_gate: zero-traffic on legacy alias for ≥1 minor version cycle
@routing
  group: A2A-intent (KEY-MGMT family wakes agent layer when client emits or receives reply)
  authority:
    KeyIssue_KeyRevoke_KeyLabel: typically operator-tier (role: main or board) — server may reject if originator lacks permission
    KeyList_KeyRenew_KeyPurge: operator-tier as well (§13.25.9) — KeyList is not an agent query; non-main agents get PERMISSION_DENIED
    AgentNameChanged: broadcast, no client authority required to receive
@deps
  ws_send: raw WS send via parent -a2a routing
  storage: optional client-side cache of last-known KeyList (UI rendering cache; invalidated on AgentNameChanged or KeyListResult)
@ports
  cmd  issue_key(label, kind?, ttlDays?)               : emit KeyIssue, await KeyIssued response
  cmd  list_keys(includeRevoked?, includeDeleted?)     : emit KeyList, await KeyListResult
  cmd  revoke_key(keyRef, mode)                        : emit KeyRevoke, await KeyRevoked
  cmd  renew_key(keyRef, ttlDays?)                     : emit KeyRenew, await KeyRenewed
  cmd  purge_revoked(keyRefs?)                         : emit KeyPurge, await KeyPurged
  cmd  label_key(keyRef, newLabel)                     : emit KeyLabel, await KeyLabeled
  out  keyIssued(key, keyRef, label, kind, expiresAt)
  out  keyListUpdated(keys[])
  out  keyRevoked(key, mode)
  out  keyRenewed(keyRef, expiresAt, wasLapsed)
  out  keyPurged(count, keyRefs)
  out  keyExpiredRefusal(phase, renewable, label, expiresAt, graceUntil?)
  out  agentNameChanged(key, oldLabel, newLabel)
@redaction
  hook: pre-send + pre-log
  targets: [issued key values (uk-* / ck-* full strings — surface only first 8 chars in logs), revoke reasons containing credential fragments]
  rationale: KEY-MGMT messages carry credential material that MUST NOT leak to public logs / committed transcripts (§13.14 redaction discipline)
@operation_discipline
  principle: KEY-MGMT is operator-tier; client gateway exposes commands but authority enforcement is server-side
  anti_patterns:
    - log full key values to non-redacted stream → credential leak
    - report a standby key (or a standby refusal received without having sent the renewal marker) to a human → it resolves on reconnect; report dormant once, revoked once (new key needed)
    - retain KeyListResult beyond UI render scope without revoke-aware invalidation → stale display + stale UX
    - emit KeyRevoke {mode: immediate} without surfacing "active session will be killed" warning to operator → unexpected disconnection
